{
  "title": "21: al-Anbiyaa الأنبياء",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-merciful, the All-compassionate\nاِقْتَرَبَ لِلنَّاسِ حِسَابُهُمْ وَهُمْ فِىْ غَفْلَةٍ مُّعْرِضُوْنَ‌ۚ‏(1)\nAEQTARABA LIN-NAASE HESAABUHUM WA HUM FEE GHAFLATIM MO’REZOON.\nCloser and closer to mankind comes their Reckoning: yet they heed not and they turn away. \nمَا يَاْتِيْهِمْ مِّنْ ذِكْرٍ مِّنْ رَّبِّہِمْ مُّحْدَثٍ اِلَّا اسْتَمَعُوْهُ وَهُمْ يَلْعَبُوْنَۙ‏(2)\nMAA YAATEEHIM MIN ZEKRIN MIN RABBEHIM MMUHDASIN ILLAA ASTAMAU’OOHU WA HUM YALA’ABOONA.\nNever comes (aught) to them of a renewed Message from their Lord, but they listen to it as in jest, \nلَاهِيَةً قُلُوْبُهُمْ‌ ؕ وَاَسَرُّوا النَّجْوَى‌ۖ الَّذِيْنَ ظَلَمُوْا ‌ۖ  هَلْ هٰذَاۤ اِلَّا بَشَرٌ مِّثْلُكُمْ‌ ۚ اَفَتَاْتُوْنَ السِّحْرَ وَاَنْتُمْ تُبْصِرُوْنَ‏(3)\nLAAHEETAN QULOOBUHUM WAASARROOA AN-NAJWAA LAZEENA ZALAMOO HAL HAAZAA ILLAA BASHARUM MISLOKUM AAFATAATOONA SEHR WA ANTUM TUBSEROON.\nTheir hearts toying as with trifles. The wrong-doers conceal their private counsels, (saying), “Is this (one) more than a man like yourselves? Will ye go to witchcraft with your eyes open?” \nقٰلَ رَبِّىْ يَعْلَمُ الْقَوْلَ فِى السَّمَآءِ وَالْاَرْضِ‌ وَهُوَ السَّمِيْعُ الْعَلِيْمُ‏(4)\nQAALA RABBEE YA’LAMO QAWLA FIL SAMAAA-E WAL ARZE WA HOWA SAMEE-U’L A’LEEM.\nSay: “My Lord knoweth (every) word (spoken) in the heavens and on earth: He is the One that heareth and knoweth (all things).” \nبَلْ قَالُوْۤا اَضْغَاثُ اَحْلَامٍۢ بَلِ افْتَرٰٮهُ بَلْ هُوَ شَاعِرٌ ‌ ۖۚ فَلْيَاْتِنَا بِاٰيَةٍ كَمَاۤ اُرْسِلَ الْاَوَّلُوْنَ‏(5)\nBAL QAALOO AAZGHAASU AAHLAAMIN BALIL AFTARAAHU BAL HOWA SHAAE’ERUN FALYAATENAA BE-AAYATIL KAMAA AURSELA AWWALOON.\n“Nay,” they say, “(these are) medleys of dream! - Nay, He forged it! - Nay, He is (but) a poet! Let him then bring us a Sign like the ones that were sent to (Prophets) of old!” \nمَاۤ اٰمَنَتْ قَبْلَهُمْ مِّنْ قَرْيَةٍ اَهْلَكْنٰهَا‌ۚ اَفَهُمْ يُؤْمِنُوْنَ‏(6)\nMAA AAAMANAT QABLAHUM MIN QARYATINW AAHLAKNAAHAA AAFAHUM YOAMENOONA.\n(As to those) before them, not one of the populations which We destroyed believed: will these believe? \nوَمَاۤ اَرْسَلْنَا قَبْلَكَ اِلَّا رِجَالًا نُّوْحِىْۤ اِلَيْهِمْ‌ فَسْئَلُوْۤا اَهْلَ الذِّكْرِ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ لَا تَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(7)\nWA MAA ARSALNAA QABLAKA ILLAA REJAALAN NNOOHEAA ELAYHIM FASALOOA AHLAL AZ-ZEKRE IN KUNTUM LAA TA’LAMOON.\nBefore thee, also, the messengers We sent were but men, to whom We granted inspiration: If ye realise this not, ask of those who possess the Message. \nوَمَا جَعَلْنٰهُمْ جَسَدًا لَّا يَاْكُلُوْنَ الطَّعَامَ وَمَا كَانُوْا خٰلِدِيْنَ‏(8)\nWA MAA JAA’ALNAAHUM JASADAN LAA YAAKOLOON TA-A’AMA WA MAA KAANOO KHAALEDEENA.\nNor did We give them bodies that ate no food, nor were they exempt from death. \nثُمَّ صَدَقْنٰهُمُ الْوَعْدَ فَاَنْجَيْنٰهُمْ وَمَنْ نَّشَآءُ وَاَهْلَكْنَا الْمُسْرِفِيْنَ‏(9)\nSUMMA SADAQNAAHUMU AL-WAA’DA FAANJAYNAAHUM WA MAN NNASHAAU WA AHLAKNAL MUSREFEEN.\nIn the end We fulfilled to them Our Promise, and We saved them and those whom We pleased, but We destroyed those who transgressed beyond bounds. \nلَقَدْ اَنْزَلْنَاۤ اِلَيْكُمْ كِتٰبًا فِيْهِ ذِكْرُكُمْ‌ؕ اَفَلَا تَعْقِلُوْنَ‏(10)\nLAQAD ANZALNAA ELAYKUM KETAABAA FEEHE ZEKRUKUM AFALAA TA’QELOON.\nWe have revealed for you (O men!) a book in which is a Message for you: will ye not then understand? \nوَكَمْ قَصَمْنَا مِنْ قَرْيَةٍ كَانَتْ ظَالِمَةً وَّاَنْشَاْنَا بَعْدَهَا قَوْمًا اٰخَرِيْنَ‏(11)\nWA QASAMNAA MIN QARYATINW KAANAT ZAALEMATAN WWAANSHAANAA BAA’DAHAA QAWMAN AAKHEREEN.\nHow many were the populations We utterly destroyed because of their iniquities, setting up in their places other peoples? \nفَلَمَّاۤ اَحَسُّوْا بَاْسَنَاۤ اِذَا هُمْ مِّنْهَا يَرْكُضُوْنَؕ‏(12)\nFALAMMAA AAHASSOOA BAASANAA EZAA HUM MINHAA YARKUZOONA.\nYet, when they felt Our Punishment (coming), behold, they (tried to) flee from it. \nلَا تَرْكُضُوْا وَ ارْجِعُوْۤا اِلٰى مَاۤ اُتْرِفْتُمْ فِيْهِ وَمَسٰكِنِكُمْ لَعَلَّكُمْ تُسْئَلُوْنَ‏(13)\nLAA TARKUZOOA WA ARJEU’OOA ELAA MAA AUTREFTUM FEEHE WAMASAAKENEKUM LA-A’LLAKUM TUS-ALOONA.\nFlee not, but return to the good things of this life which were given you, and to your homes in order that ye may be called to account. \nقَالُوْا يٰوَيْلَنَاۤ اِنَّا كُنَّا ظٰلِمِيْنَ‏(14)\nQAALOO YAA WAYLANAA INNAA KUNNAA ZAALEMEEN.\nThey said: “Ah! woe to us! We were indeed wrong-doers!” \nفَمَا زَالَتْ تِّلْكَ دَعْوٰٮهُمْ حَتّٰى جَعَلْنٰهُمْ حَصِيْدًا خٰمِدِيْنَ‏(15)\nFAMAA ZAALAT TTELKA DAA’WAAHUM HATTAA JAA’ALNAAHUM HASEEDAN KHAAMEDEENA.\nAnd that cry of theirs ceased not, till We made them as a field that is mown, as ashes silent and quenched. \nوَمَا خَلَقْنَا السَّمَآءَ وَالْاَرْضَ وَمَا بَيْنَهُمَا لٰعِبِيْنَ‏(16)\nWA MAA KHALAQNAL SAMAAA-AD WAL ARZA WA MAA BAYNAHOMAA LAA-E’BEEN.\nNot for (idle) sport did We create the heavens and the earth and all that is between! \nلَوْ اَرَدْنَاۤ اَنْ نَّتَّخِذَ لَهْوًا لَّا تَّخَذْنٰهُ مِنْ لَّدُنَّاۤ  ۖ  اِنْ كُنَّا فٰعِلِيْنَ‏(17)\nLAW AARADNAA AN NNATTAKHEZA LAHWAN LAA TTAKHAZNAAHU MIN WA IN KUNNAA FAAE’ELEENA.\nIf it had been Our wish to take (just) a pastime, We should surely have taken it from the things nearest to Us, if We would do (such a thing)! \nبَلْ نَقْذِفُ بِالْحَقِّ عَلَى الْبَاطِلِ فَيَدْمَغُهٗ فَاِذَا هُوَ زَاهِقٌ‌ ؕ وَلَكُمُ الْوَيْلُ مِمَّا تَصِفُوْنَ‏(18)\nBAL NAQZEFU BIL-HAQQE A’LAL AL-BAATELE FAYADMAGHUH FA-EZAA HOWA ZAAHEQUN WA LAKOMUL AL-WAYLU MIMMAA TASEFOONA.\nNay, We hurl the Truth against falsehood, and it knocks out its brain, and behold, falsehood doth perish! Ah! woe be to you for the (false) things ye ascribe (to Us). \nوَلَهٗ مَنْ فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ‌ؕ وَمَنْ عِنْدَهٗ لَا يَسْتَكْبِرُوْنَ عَنْ عِبَادَتِهٖ وَلَا يَسْتَحْسِرُوْنَ‌ۚ‏(19)\nWA LAHU MAN FIL SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZ WA MAN I’NDAHU LAA YASTAKBEROONA A’N E’EBAADATEH WA LAA YASTAHSEROONA.\nTo Him belong all (creatures) in the heavens and on earth: Even those who are in His (very) Presence are not too proud to serve Him, nor are they (ever) weary (of His service): \nيُسَبِّحُوْنَ الَّيْلَ وَالنَّهَارَ لَا يَفْتُرُوْنَ‏(20)\nYUSABBEHOONA LAYLA WAN NAHAARA LAA YAFTUROONA.\nThey celebrate His praises night and day, nor do they ever flag or intermit. \nاَمِ اتَّخَذُوْۤا اٰلِهَةً مِّنَ الْاَرْضِ هُمْ يُنْشِرُوْنَ‏(21)\nAMIL ATTAKHAZOOA AALEHATAL MENAL ARZE HUM YUNSHEROONA.\nOr have they taken (for worship) gods from the earth who can raise (the dead)? \nلَوْ كَانَ فِيْهِمَاۤ اٰلِهَةٌ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ لَفَسَدَتَا‌ۚ فَسُبْحٰنَ اللّٰهِ رَبِّ الْعَرْشِ عَمَّا يَصِفُوْنَ‏(22)\nLAW KAANA FEEHEMAA AAALEHATUN ILLAA LAAHO LAFASADATAA FA-SUBHAANAL LAAHE RABBE A’RSHIL A’MMAA YASEFOONA.\nIf there were, in the heavens and the earth, other gods besides Allah, there would have been confusion in both! but glory to Allah, the Lord of the Throne: (High is He) above what they attribute to Him! \nلَا يُسْئَلُ عَمَّا يَفْعَلُ وَهُمْ يُسْئَلُوْنَ‏(23)\nLAA YUSALO A’MMAA YAF-A’LO WA HUM YUSALOONA.\nHe cannot be questioned for His acts, but they will be questioned (for theirs). \nاَمِ اتَّخَذُوْا مِنْ دُوْنِهٖۤ اٰلِهَةً ‌ ؕ قُلْ هَاتُوْا بُرْهَانَكُمْ‌ ۚ هٰذَا ذِكْرُ مَنْ مَّعِىَ وَذِكْرُ مَنْ قَبْلِىْ‌ ؕ بَلْ اَكْثَرُهُمْ لَا يَعْلَمُوْنَ ۙ الْحَقَّ‌ فَهُمْ مُّعْرِضُوْنَ‏(24)\nAMIL ATTAKHAZOOA MIN DOONEHI AALEHATAL QUL HAATOO BURHAANAKUM HAAZAA ZEKRU MAN MA-E’YA WAZEKRU MAN QABLEAA BAL AKSAROHUM LAA YA’LAMOON HAQQA FAHUM MO’REZOON.\nOr have they taken for worship (other) gods besides him? Say, “Bring your convincing proof: this is the Message of those with me and the Message of those before me.” But most of them know not the Truth, and so turn away. \nوَمَاۤ اَرْسَلْنَا مِنْ قَبْلِكَ مِنْ رَّسُوْلٍ اِلَّا نُوْحِىْۤ اِلَيْهِ اَنَّهٗ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّاۤ اَنَا فَاعْبُدُوْنِ‏(25)\nWA MAA ARSALNAA MIN QABLEKA MIN RASOOLIN ILLAA NOOHEAA ELAYHE ANNAHU LAA ELAAHA ILLAA ANAA FA’BODOON.\nNot a messenger did We send before thee without this inspiration sent by Us to him: that there is no god but I; therefore worship and serve Me. \nوَقَالُوا اتَّخَذَ الرَّحْمٰنُ وَلَدًا‌ سُبْحٰنَهٗ‌ ؕ بَلْ عِبَادٌ مُّكْرَمُوْنَ ۙ‏(26)\nWA TAKHAZA RAHMAANO LAAHO WALADAN BAL E’EBAADUN MMUKRAMOONA.\nAnd they say: The Beneficent Allah has taken to Himself a son. Glory be to Him. Nay! they are honored servants \nلَا يَسْبِقُوْنَهٗ بِالْقَوْلِ وَهُمْ بِاَمْرِهٖ يَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(27)\nLAA YASBEQOONAH BIL-QAWLE WA HUM LAAHO YA’MALOON.\nThey do not precede Him in speech and (only) according to His commandment do they act. \nيَعْلَمُ مَا بَيْنَ اَيْدِيْهِمْ وَمَا خَلْفَهُمْ وَ لَا يَشْفَعُوْنَۙ اِلَّا لِمَنِ ارْتَضٰى وَهُمْ مِّنْ خَشْيَتِهٖ مُشْفِقُوْنَ‏(28)\nYA’LAMO MAA BAYNA AYDEEHIM WA MAA KHALFAHUM WA LAA YASHFAU’OONA ILLAA LEMANIT ARTAZAA WA HUM MIN KHASHYATEH MUSHFEQOONA.\nHe knows what is before them and what is behind them, and they do not intercede except for him whom He approves and for fear of Him they tremble. \nوَمَنْ يَّقُلْ مِنْهُمْ اِنِّىْۤ اِلٰهٌ مِّنْ دُوْنِهٖ فَذٰلِكَ نَجْزِيْهِ جَهَنَّمَ‌ؕ كَذٰلِكَ نَجْزِى الظّٰلِمِيْنَ‏(29)\nWA MAN YYAQUL MINHUM INNEE ELAAHUN MIN DOONEHI FA-ZAALEKAL NAJZEEHE JAHANNAM KAZAALEKA NAJZIL ZAALEMEEN.\nIf any of them should say, “I am a god besides Him”, such a one We should reward with Hell: thus do We reward those who do wrong. \nاَوَلَمْ يَرَ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْۤا اَنَّ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضَ كَانَتَا رَتْقًا فَفَتَقْنٰهُمَا‌ ؕ وَجَعَلْنَا مِنَ الْمَآءِ كُلَّ شَىْءٍ حَىٍّ‌ ؕ اَفَلَا يُؤْمِنُوْنَ‏(30)\nAWALAM YARAL LAZEENA KAFAROO ANNAL SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZA KAANATAA RATQAN FAFATAQNAAHUMAA WA JA-A’LNAA MENAL AL-MAAE KULLA SHAY-IN HAA AFALAA YOAMENOONA.\nDo not the Unbelievers see that the heavens and the earth were joined together (as one unit of creation), before we clove them asunder? We made from water every living thing. Will they not then believe? \nوَجَعَلْنَا فِى الْاَرْضِ رَوَاسِىَ اَنْ تَمِيْدَ بِهِمْ وَجَعَلْنَا فِيْهَا فِجَاجًا سُبُلًا لَّعَلَّهُمْ يَهْتَدُوْنَ‏(31)\nWA JA-A’LNAA FIL ARZE JA-A’LA AN TAMEEDA BEHIM WA JA-A’LNAA FEEHAA FEJAAJAN SUBULAN LA-A’LLAHUM YAHTADOON.\nAnd We have set on the earth mountains standing firm, lest it should shake with them, and We have made therein broad highways (between mountains) for them to pass through: that they may receive Guidance. \nوَجَعَلْنَا السَّمَآءَ سَقْفًا مَّحْفُوْظًا ۖۚ وَّهُمْ عَنْ اٰيٰتِهَا مُعْرِضُوْنَ‏(32)\nWA JA-A’LNAA SAMAAA-AD SAQFAN MMAHFOOZAN WA HUM A’N AAAYAATEHAA MUA’REZOONA.\nAnd We have made the heavens as a canopy well guarded: yet do they turn away from the Signs which these things (point to)! \nوَهُوَ الَّذِىْ خَلَقَ الَّيْلَ وَالنَّهَارَ وَالشَّمْسَ وَالْقَمَرَ‌ؕ كُلٌّ فِىْ فَلَكٍ يَّسْبَحُوْنَ‏(33)\nWA HOWA LAZEE KHALAQAL LAYLA WAN NAHAARA WA SHAMSA WAL QAMARA KULLUL FEE FALAKINY YASBAHOON.\nIt is He Who created the Night and the Day, and the sun and the moon: all (the celestial bodies) swim along, each in its rounded course. \nوَمَا جَعَلْنَا لِبَشَرٍ مِّنْ قَبْلِكَ الْخُلْدَ‌ ؕ اَفَا۟ئِن مِّتَّ فَهُمُ الْخٰلِدُوْنَ‏(34)\nWA MAA JA-A’LNAA LEBASHARIN MIN QABLEKA AL-KHULDA AAFAAEN MMETTA FA HOMUL AL-KHAALEDOONA.\nWe granted not to any man before thee permanent life (here): if then thou shouldst die, would they live permanently? \nكُلُّ نَفْسٍ ذَآئِقَةُ الْمَوْتِ‌ؕ وَنَبْلُوْكُمْ بِالشَّرِّ وَالْخَيْرِ فِتْنَةً‌  ؕ وَاِلَيْنَا تُرْجَعُوْنَ‏(35)\nKULLO NAFSIM ZAAA-EQATUL MAWT WANABLOOKUM BEALSSHARRE WA KHAYR FETNATAN WA ELAYNAA TURJA-O’ON.\nEvery soul shall have a taste of death: and We test you by evil and by good by way of trial. to Us must ye return. \nوَاِذَا رَاٰكَ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْۤا اِنْ يَّتَّخِذُوْنَكَ اِلَّا هُزُوًا ؕ اَهٰذَا الَّذِىْ يَذْكُرُ اٰلِهَتَكُمْ‌ۚ وَهُمْ بِذِكْرِ الرَّحْمٰنِ هُمْ كٰفِرُوْنَ‏(36)\nWA EZAA RAAKA LAZEENA KAFAROO IN YYATTAKHEZOONAKA ILLAA HOZOWANW AAHAAZAA LAZEE YAZKURU AAALEHATAKUM WA HUM BE-ELAA RAHMAANIR HUM KAAFEROON.\nWhen the Unbelievers see thee, they treat thee not except with ridicule. “Is this,” (they say), “the one who talks of your gods?” and they blaspheme at the mention of (Allah) Most Gracious! \nخُلِقَ الْاِنْسَانُ مِنْ عَجَلٍ‌ؕ سَاُورِيْكُمْ اٰيٰتِىْ فَلَا تَسْتَعْجِلُوْنِ‏(37)\nKHOLEQA INSAANO MIN A’AJALIN SAAWREEKUM AAAYAATEAA FALAA TASTAA’JELOONE.\nMan is a creature of haste: soon (enough) will I show you My Signs; then ye will not ask Me to hasten them! \nوَيَقُوْلُوْنَ مَتٰى هٰذَا الْوَعْدُ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ صٰدِقِيْنَ‏(38)\nWA YAQOOLOONA MATAA HAAZAA WA’DO IN KUNTUM SAADEQEEN.\nThey say: “When will this promise come to pass, if ye are telling the truth?” \nلَوْ يَعْلَمُ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا حِيْنَ لَا يَكُفُّوْنَ عَنْ وُّجُوْهِهِمُ النَّارَ وَلَا عَنْ ظُهُوْرِهِمْ وَلَا هُمْ يُنْصَرُوْنَ‏(39)\nLAW YA’LAMO LAZEENA KAFAROO HEENA LAA YAKUFFOONA A’N WWUJOOHEHEMU NAARAL WA LAA A’N ZOHOOREHIM WA LAA HUM HUM YUNSAROON.\nIf only the Unbelievers knew (the time) when they will not be able to ward off the fire from their faces, nor yet from their backs, and (when) no help can reach them! \nبَلْ تَاْتِيْهِمْ بَغْتَةً فَتَبْهَتُهُمْ فَلَا يَسْتَطِيْعُوْنَ رَدَّهَا وَلَا هُمْ يُنْظَرُوْنَ‏(40)\nBAL TAA-TEEHIM BAGHTATANW FATABHATUHUM FALAA YASTATEE-O’ONA RADDAHAA WA LAA HUM HUM YUNZAROON.\nNay, it may come to them all of a sudden and confound them: no power will they have then to avert it, nor will they (then) get respite. \nوَلَقَدِ اسْتُهْزِئَ بِرُسُلٍ مِّنْ قَبْلِكَ فَحَاقَ بِالَّذِيْنَ سَخِرُوْا مِنْهُمْ مَّا كَانُوْا بِهٖ يَسْتَهْزِءُوْنَ‏(41)\nLAQADIS ASTUHZEA BERUSULIN MIN QABLEKA FAHAAQA BE-LAZEENA SAKHEROOA MINHUM MAA KAANOO BEHI YASTAHZEOON.\nMocked were (many) messenger before thee; But their scoffers were hemmed in by the thing that they mocked. \nقُلْ مَنْ يَّكْلَؤُكُمْ بِالَّيْلِ وَالنَّهَارِ مِنَ الرَّحْمٰنِ‌ؕ بَلْ هُمْ عَنْ ذِكْرِ رَبِّهِمْ مُّعْرِضُوْنَ‏(42)\nQUL MAN YYAKLAUKUM BIL-LAYLE WAN NAHAARE MENAL RAHMAAN BAL HUM A’N ELAA RABBEHIM MO’REZOON.\nSay: “Who can keep you safe by night and by day from (the Wrath of) (Allah) Most Gracious?” Yet they turn away from the mention of their Lord. \nاَمْ لَهُمْ اٰلِهَةٌ تَمْنَعُهُمْ مِّنْ دُوْنِنَا ‌ؕ لَا يَسْتَطِيْعُوْنَ نَصْرَ اَنْفُسِهِمْ وَلَا هُمْ مِّنَّا يُصْحَبُوْنَ‏(43)\nAM LAHUM AAALEHATUN TAMNAU’UHUM MIN DOONENAA LAA YASTATEE-O’ONA NASRAL ANFOSEHIM WA LAA HUM MINNAA YUSHABOONA.\nOr have they gods that can guard them from Us? They have no power to aid themselves, nor can they be defended from Us. \nبَلْ مَتَّعْنَا هٰٓؤُلَاۤءِ وَ اٰبَآءَهُمْ حَتّٰى طَالَ عَلَيْهِمُ الْعُمُرُ ‌ؕ اَفَلَا يَرَوْنَ اَنَّا نَاْتِى الْاَرْضَ نَنْقُصُهَا مِنْ اَطْرَافِهَا ؕ‌ اَفَهُمُ الْغٰلِبُوْنَ‏(44)\nBAL MATTAA’NAA HAAOOLAAA-E WA AA-BAAA-AHUM HATTAA TAALA A’LAYHEMUL O’MOR AFALAA YARAWNAL ANNAA NAATEAA ARZA NANQUSUHAA MIN AATRAAFEHAA AAFAHUMU GHAALEBOON.\nNay, We gave the good things of this life to these men and their fathers until the period grew long for them; See they not that We gradually reduce the land (in their control) from its outlying borders? Is it then they who will win? \nقُلْ اِنَّمَاۤ اُنْذِرُكُمْ بِالْوَحْىِ ‌‌ۖ  وَلَا يَسْمَعُ الصُّمُّ الدُّعَآءَ اِذَا مَا يُنْذَرُوْنَ‏(45)\nQUL INNAMAA AUNZERUKUM BIL-WAHAAE WA LAA YASMA-O’ AS-SUMMU DO-A’AA-A EZAA MAA YUNZAROONA.\nSay, “I do but warn you according to revelation”: But the deaf will not hear the call, (even) when they are warned! \nوَلَئِنْ مَّسَّتْهُمْ نَفْحَةٌ مِّنْ عَذَابِ رَبِّكَ لَيَقُوْلُنَّ يٰوَيْلَنَاۤ اِنَّا كُنَّا ظٰلِمِيْنَ‏(46)\nWA LAIN MMASSATHUM NAFHATUN MIN A’ZAABIN RABBEKA LAYAQOOLUNNAL YAA WAYLANAA INNAA KUNNAA ZAALEMEEN.\nIf but a breath of the Wrath of thy Lord do touch them, they will then say, “Woe to us! we did wrong indeed!” \nوَنَضَعُ الْمَوَازِيْنَ الْقِسْطَ لِيَوْمِ الْقِيٰمَةِ فَلَا تُظْلَمُ نَفْسٌ شَيْئًا‌ ؕ وَاِنْ كَانَ مِثْقَالَ حَبَّةٍ مِّنْ خَرْدَلٍ اَتَيْنَا بِهَا‌ ؕ وَكَفٰى بِنَا حٰسِبِيْنَ‏(47)\nWANAZAU’U AL-MAWAAZEENA AL-QESTA LE-YAWMIL QEYAAMATE FALAA TUZLAMO NAFSUN SHAY-ANW WA KAANA MISQAALA HABBATIN MIN KHARDALIN ATAYNAA BEHAA KAFAA LAKHASAFA HAASEBEENA.\nWe shall set up scales of justice for the Day of Judgment, so that not a soul will be dealt with unjustly in the least, and if there be (no more than) the weight of a mustard seed, We will bring it (to account): and enough are We to take account. \nوَلَقَدْ اٰتَيْنَا مُوْسٰى وَهٰرُوْنَ الْفُرْقَانَ وَضِيَآءً وَّذِكْرًا لِّلْمُتَّقِيْنَۙ‏(48)\nWA LAQAD AATAYNAA MOOSAA WA AALO AL-FURQAANA WAZEEAAAAN WWAZEKRAN LIL-MUTTAQEEN.\nIn the past We granted to Moses and Aaron the criterion (for judgment), and a Light and a Message for those who would do right, \nالَّذِيْنَ يَخْشَوْنَ رَبَّهُمْ بِالْغَيْبِ وَهُمْ مِّنَ السَّاعَةِ مُشْفِقُوْنَ‏(49)\nLAZEENA YAKHSHAWNA RABBAHUM BIL-GHAYBE WA HUM MENAL AS-SAAA’ATE MUSHFEQOONA.\nThose who fear their Lord in their most secret thoughts, and who hold the Hour (of Judgment) in awe. \nوَهٰذَا ذِكْرٌ مُّبٰرَكٌ اَنْزَلْنٰهُ‌ؕ اَفَاَنْتُمْ لَهٗ مُنْكِرُوْنَ‏(50)\nWA ZIKRUNW MMUBAARAKUN AANZALNAAHU AAFAANTUM LAHU MUNKEROONA.\nAnd this is a blessed Message which We have sent down: will ye then reject it? \nوَلَقَدْ اٰتَيْنَاۤ اِبْرٰهِيْمَ رُشْدَهٗ مِنْ قَبْلُ وَ كُنَّا بِهٖ عٰلِمِيْنَ‌ۚ‏(51)\nWA LAQAD AATAYNAA IBRAAHEEMA RUSHDAH MIN QABLO WA KUNNAA BEHI A’AALEMEENA.\nWe bestowed aforetime on Abraham his rectitude of conduct, and well were We acquainted with him. \nاِذْ قَالَ لِاَبِيْهِ وَقَوْمِهٖ مَا هٰذِهِ التَّمَاثِيْلُ الَّتِىْۤ اَنْتُمْ لَهَا عٰكِفُوْنَ‏(52)\nIZ QAALA LEAABEEHE WA QAWMEHI MAA HAAZEHE AT-TAMAASEELU LATEE ANTUM LAHAA ANTUM.\nBehold! he said to his father and his people, “What are these images, to which ye are (so assiduously) devoted?” \nقَالُوْا وَجَدْنَاۤ اٰبَآءَنَا لَهَا عٰبِدِيْنَ‏(53)\nQAALOO WAJADNAA AABAAA-ANAA LAHAA A’AABEDEENA.\nThey said, “We found our fathers worshipping them.” \nقَالَ لَقَدْ كُنْتُمْ اَنْتُمْ وَاٰبَآؤُكُمْ فِىْ ضَلٰلٍ مُّبِيْنٍ‏(54)\nQAALA LAQAD KUNTUM ANTUM WAABAAUKUM FEE ZALAALIM MOBEEN.\nHe said, “Indeed ye have been in manifest error - ye and your fathers.” \nقَالُوْۤا اَجِئْتَنَا بِالْحَقِّ اَمْ اَنْتَ مِنَ اللّٰعِبِيْنَ‏(55)\nQAALOO AAJETANAA BIL-HAQQE AM ANTA MENAL AL-LAAE’EBEENA.\nThey said, “Have you brought us the Truth, or are you one of those who jest?” \nقَالَ بَلْ رَّبُّكُمْ رَبُّ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ الَّذِىْ فَطَرَهُنَّ ‌ۖ  وَاَنَا عَلٰى ذٰلِكُمْ مِّنَ الشّٰهِدِيْنَ‏(56)\nQAALA BAL RRABBUKUM RABBUL SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZE LAZEE FATARAHUNNA ANAT A’LAA ZAALEKUM MENAL SHAAHEDEEN.\nHe said, “Nay, your Lord is the Lord of the heavens and the earth, He Who created them (from nothing): and I am a witness to this (Truth). \nوَ تَاللّٰهِ لَاَكِيْدَنَّ اَصْنَامَكُمْ بَعْدَ اَنْ تُوَلُّوْا مُدْبِرِيْنَ‏(57)\nWA TAALLLAAHE LAAKEEDANNA AASNAAMAKUM BA’DA AN TOWALLOO MUDBEREEN.\n“And by Allah, I have a plan for your idols - after ye go away and turn your backs”.. \nفَجَعَلَهُمْ جُذٰذًا اِلَّا كَبِيْرًا لَّهُمْ لَعَلَّهُمْ اِلَيْهِ يَرْجِعُوْنَ‏(58)\nFA-JA-A’LAHUM JUZAAZAN ILLAA KABEERAA LAHUM LA-A’LLAHUM ELAYHE YARJE-O’ON.\nSo he broke them to pieces, (all) but the biggest of them, that they might turn (and address themselves) to it. \nقَالُوْا مَنْ فَعَلَ هٰذَا بِاٰلِهَتِنَاۤ اِنَّهٗ لَمِنَ الظّٰلِمِيْنَ‏(59)\nQAALOO MAN FA-A’LA HAAZAA BEAAALEHATENAA INNAHU LAMENAS ZAALEMEEN.\nThey said, “Who has done this to our gods? He must indeed be some man of impiety!” \nقَالُوْا سَمِعْنَا فَتًى يَّذْكُرُهُمْ يُقَالُ لَهٗۤ اِبْرٰهِيْمُ ؕ‏(60)\nQAALOO SAMEA’NAA FATAN YYAZKURUHUM YOQAALO LAHU AEBRAAHEEMU.\nThey said, “We heard a youth talk of them: He is called Abraham.” \nقَالُوْا فَاْتُوْا بِهٖ عَلٰٓى اَعْيُنِ النَّاسِ لَعَلَّهُمْ يَشْهَدُوْنَ‏(61)\nQAALOO FAATOO BEHI A’LAA AAA’YUNE NAASE LA-A’LLAHUM YASHHADOONA.\nThey said, “Then bring him before the eyes of the people, that they may bear witness.” \nقَالُوْٓا ءَاَنْتَ فَعَلْتَ هٰذَا بِاٰلِهَتِنَا يٰۤاِبْرٰهِيْمُؕ‏(62)\nA-TAJ-A’LO AANTA FAA’ALTA HAAZAA BEAAALEHATENAA YAABRAAHEEMU.\nThey said, “Art thou the one that did this with our gods, O Abraham?” \nقَالَ بَلْ فَعَلَهٗ ‌‌ۖ  كَبِيْرُهُمْ هٰذَا فَسْئَلُوْهُمْ اِنْ كَانُوْا يَنْطِقُوْنَ‏(63)\nQAALA BAL FAA’ALAH KABEERUHUM HAAZAA FASALOOHUM IN KAANOO YANTEQOON.\nHe said: “Nay, this was done by - this is their biggest one! ask them, if they can speak intelligently!” \nفَرَجَعُوْۤا اِلٰٓى اَنْفُسِهِمْ فَقَالُوْۤا اِنَّكُمْ اَنْتُمُ الظّٰلِمُوْنَۙ‏(64)\nFARAJAU’OOA ELAA ANFOSEHIM FA-QAALOO INNAKUM AANTUMU ZAALEMOON.\nSo they turned to themselves and said, “Surely ye are the ones in the wrong!” \nثُمَّ نُكِسُوْا عَلٰى رُءُوْسِہِمْ‌ۚ لَقَدْ عَلِمْتَ مَا هٰٓؤُلَاۤءِ يَنْطِقُوْنَ‏(65)\nSUMMA NUKESOOA A’LAA RUOOSEHEM LAQAD A’ALEMTA MAA HAAOOLAAA-E YANTEQOON.\nThen were they confounded with shame: (they said), “Thou knowest full well that these (idols) do not speak!” \nقَالَ اَفَتَعْبُدُوْنَ مِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ مَا لَا يَنْفَعُكُمْ شَيْئًا وَّلَا يَضُرُّكُمْؕ‏(66)\nQAALA AAFATAA’BUDOONA MIN DOONIL LAAHE MAA LAA YANFAU’UKUM SHAY-ANW WA LAA YAZURRUKUM.\n(Abraham) said, “Do ye then worship, besides Allah, things that can neither be of any good to you nor do you harm? \nاُفٍّ لَّكُمْ وَلِمَا تَعْبُدُوْنَ مِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ‌ؕ اَفَلَا تَعْقِلُوْنَ‏(67)\nAUFFIN LAKUM WA LEMAKH TA’BODOONA MIN DOONIL LAAH AFALAA TA’QELOON.\n“Fie upon you, and upon the things that ye worship besides Allah! Have ye no sense?”.. \nقَالُوْا حَرِّقُوْهُ وَانْصُرُوْۤا اٰلِهَتَكُمْ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ فٰعِلِيْنَ‏(68)\nQAALOO HARREQOOHU WAANSUROOA AAALEHATAKUM IN KUNTUM FAAE’ELEENA.\nThey said, “Burn him and protect your gods, If ye do (anything at all)!” \nقُلْنَا يٰنَارُ كُوْنِىْ بَرْدًا وَّسَلٰمًا عَلٰٓى اِبْرٰهِيْمَۙ‏(69)\nQULNAL YAA NAARUL KOONEAA BARDANW WWASALAAMAN A’LAA IBRAAHEEMA.\nWe said, “O Fire! be thou cool, and (a means of) safety for Abraham!” \nوَاَرَادُوْا بِهٖ كَيْدًا فَجَعَلْنٰهُمُ الْاَخْسَرِيْنَ‌ۚ‏(70)\nWAARAADOOA BEHI KAYDAANW FAJAA’ALNAAHUMU AL-AAKHSAREENA.\nThen they sought a stratagem against him: but We made them the ones that lost most! \nوَنَجَّيْنٰهُ وَلُوْطًا اِلَى الْاَرْضِ الَّتِىْ بٰرَكْنَا فِيْهَا لِلْعٰلَمِيْنَ‏(71)\nWANAJJAYNAAHU WA LOOTAN ELAL ARZE LATEE BAARAKNAA FEEHAA LIL-A’AALAMEENA.\nBut We delivered him and (his nephew) Lut (and directed them) to the land which We have blessed for the nations. \nوَوَهَبْنَا لَهٗۤ اِسْحٰقَ ؕ وَيَعْقُوْبَ نَافِلَةً‌  ؕ وَكُلًّا جَعَلْنَا صٰلِحِيْنَ‏(72)\nWA WAHABNAA LAHU ISHAAQA WA YA’QOOBA NAAFELATAN WAKULLAN JA-A’LNAA SAALEHEENA.\nAnd We bestowed on him Isaac and, as an additional gift, (a grandson), Jacob, and We made righteous men of every one (of them). \nوَجَعَلْنٰهُمْ اَئِمَّةً يَّهْدُوْنَ بِاَمْرِنَا وَاَوْحَيْنَاۤ اِلَيْهِمْ فِعْلَ الْخَيْرٰتِ وَاِقَامَ الصَّلٰوةِ وَاِيْتَآءَ الزَّكٰوةِ‌ۚ وَكَانُوْا لَنَا عٰبِدِيْنَ ۙ‌ۚ‏(73)\nWA JA-A’LNAAHUM AIMMATAWN YYAHDOONA BEAAMRENAA WA AWHAYNAA ELAYHIM FEA’LA AL-KHAYRAATE WAAQAAMA AS-SALAAWTE WAAYTAAA AZ-ZAKAAWTE WA KAANOO LANAA A’AABEDEENA.\nAnd We made them leaders, guiding (men) by Our Command, and We sent them inspiration to do good deeds, to establish regular prayers, and to practise regular charity; and they constantly served Us (and Us only). \nوَلُوْطًا اٰتَيْنٰهُ حُكْمًا وَّعِلْمًا وَّنَجَّيْنٰهُ مِنَ الْقَرْيَةِ الَّتِىْ كَانَتْ تَّعْمَلُ الْخَبٰٓئِثَ‌ؕ اِنَّهُمْ كَانُوْا قَوْمَ سَوْءٍ فٰسِقِيْنَۙ‏(74)\nWA LOOTAN AATAYNAAHO HUKMAWN WA I’LMAA WWANAJJAYNAAHU MENAL QARYAH LATEE KAANAT TTAA’MALU AL-KHABAAAESA INNAHUM KAANOO QAWMA SAWIN FAASEQEEN.\nAnd to Lut, too, We gave Judgment and Knowledge, and We saved him from the town which practised abominations: truly they were a people given to Evil, a rebellious people. \nوَاَدْخَلْنٰهُ فِىْ رَحْمَتِنَا‌ ؕ اِنَّهٗ مِنَ الصّٰلِحِيْنَ‏(75)\nWAADKHALNAAHU FEE RAHMATENAA INNAHU MENAL SAALEHEEN.\nAnd We admitted him to Our Mercy: for he was one of the Righteous. \nوَنُوْحًا اِذْ نَادٰى مِنْ قَبْلُ فَاسْتَجَبْنَا لَهٗ فَنَجَّيْنٰهُ وَاَهْلَهٗ مِنَ الْكَرْبِ الْعَظِيْمِ‌ۚ‏(76)\nWA ARSALNAA IZ NAADAA MIN QABLO FAASTAJABNAA LAHU FANAJJAYNAAHU AHLAHU MENAL AL-KARBE A’ZEEM.\n(Remember) Noah, when he cried (to Us) aforetime: We listened to his (prayer) and delivered him and his family from great distress. \nوَنَصَرْنٰهُ مِنَ الْقَوْمِ الَّذِيْنَ كَذَّبُوْا بِاٰيٰتِنَا ‌ؕ اِنَّهُمْ كَانُوْا قَوْمَ سَوْءٍ فَاَغْرَقْنٰهُمْ اَجْمَعِيْنَ‏(77)\nWANASARNAAHU MENAL QAWMIL LAZEENA KAZZABOO BE-AAYAATENAA INNAHUM KAANOO QAWMA SAWIN FAAGHRAQNAAHUM AJMA-E’ENA.\nWe helped him against people who rejected Our Signs: truly they were a people given to Evil: so We drowned them (in the Flood) all together. \nوَدَاوٗدَ وَسُلَيْمٰنَ اِذْ يَحْكُمٰنِ فِى الْحَرْثِ اِذْ نَفَشَتْ فِيْهِ غَنَمُ الْقَوْمِ‌ۚ وَكُنَّا لِحُكْمِهِمْ شٰهِدِيْنَ ۙ‏(78)\nWA DAAWOODA WA SOLAYMAANA IZ YAHKUMAANE FIL AL-HARSE IZ NAFASHAT FEEHE GHANAMU QAWMIL KUNNAA LEHUKMEHEM SHAAHEDEENA.\nAnd remember David and Solomon, when they gave judgment in the matter of the field into which the sheep of certain people had strayed by night: We did witness their judgment. \nفَفَهَّمْنٰهَا سُلَيْمٰنَ‌‌ۚ وَكُلًّا اٰتَيْنَا حُكْمًا وَّعِلْمًا‌ وَّسَخَّرْنَا مَعَ دَاوٗدَ الْجِبَالَ يُسَبِّحْنَ وَالطَّيْرَ‌ ؕ وَكُنَّا فٰعِلِيْنَ‏(79)\nFAFAHHAMNAAHAA SOLAYMAANA WAKULLAN AATAYNAA HUKMAWN WA I’LMAA WWASAKKHARNAA LAAHA DAAWOODA JEBAALA YUSABBEHNA WA TAYRA KUNNAA FAAE’ELEENA.\nTo Solomon We inspired the (right) understanding of the matter: to each (of them) We gave Judgment and Knowledge; it was Our power that made the hills and the birds celebrate Our praises, with David: it was We Who did (all these things). \nوَعَلَّمْنٰهُ صَنْعَةَ لَبُوْسٍ لَّكُمْ لِتُحْصِنَكُمْ مِّنْۢ بَاْسِكُمْ‌ۚ فَهَلْ اَنْتُمْ شٰكِرُوْنَ‏(80)\nWA A’LLAMNAAHUSH-SHE’RA SANA’ATA LABOOSIN LAKUM LETUHSENAKUM MIN BAASEKUM FA HAL ANTUM SHAAKEROONA.\nIt was We Who taught him the making of coats of mail for your benefit, to guard you from each other's violence: will ye then be grateful? \nوَلِسُلَيْمٰنَ الرِّيْحَ عَاصِفَةً تَجْرِىْ بِاَمْرِهٖۤ اِلَى الْاَرْضِ الَّتِىْ بٰرَكْنَا فِيْهَا‌ؕ وَكُنَّا بِكُلِّ شَىْءٍ عٰلِمِيْنَ‏(81)\nWA LESOLAYMAANA AR-REEHA A’AASEFATAN TAJREE LAAHO ELAL ARZE LATEE BAARAKNAA FEEHAA KUNNAA BEKULLE SHAY-IN A’AALEMEENA.\n(It was Our power that made) the violent (unruly) wind flow (tamely) for Solomon, to his order, to the land which We had blessed: for We do know all things. \nوَمِنَ الشَّيٰطِيْنِ مَنْ يَّغُوْصُوْنَ لَهٗ وَيَعْمَلُوْنَ عَمَلًا دُوْنَ ذٰ لِكَ‌ ۚ وَكُنَّا لَهُمْ حٰفِظِيْنَۙ‏(82)\nWA MENAN ASH-SHAYTEENE MAN YYAGHOOSOONA LAHU WA YA’MALOON A’AMALAN DOONA ZAA LEKA KUNNAA LAHUM HAAFEZEEN.\nAnd of the evil ones, were some who dived for him, and did other work besides; and it was We Who guarded them. \nوَاَيُّوْبَ اِذْ نَادٰى رَبَّهٗۤ اَنِّىْ مَسَّنِىَ الضُّرُّ وَاَنْتَ اَرْحَمُ الرّٰحِمِيْنَ‌ ۖ‌ۚ‏(83)\nWAAYYOOBA IZ NAADAA WAL AANNEAA MASSANEAAA AZ-ZURRU WA ANTA AARHAMU AR-RAAHEMEENA.\nAnd (remember) Job, when He cried to his Lord, “Truly distress has seized me, but Thou art the Most Merciful of those that are merciful.” \nفَاسْتَجَبْنَا لَهٗ فَكَشَفْنَا مَا بِهٖ مِنْ ضُرٍّ‌ وَّاٰتَيْنٰهُ اَهْلَهٗ و مِثْلَهُمْ مَّعَهُمْ رَحْمَةً مِّنْ عِنْدِنَا وَذِكْرٰى لِلْعٰبِدِيْنَ‏(84)\nFAASTAJABNAA LAHU FAKASHAFNAA MAA BEHI MIN ZURRIN WWAATAYNAAHU AHLAHU W MESLAHUM MMAA’AHUM RAHMATAM MIN I’NDENAA WAZEKRAA LIL-A’AABEDEENA.\nSo We listened to him: We removed the distress that was on him, and We restored his people to him, and doubled their number, as a Grace from Ourselves, and a thing for commemoration, for all who serve Us. \nوَاِسْمٰعِيْلَ وَاِدْرِيْسَ وَذَا الْكِفْلِ‌ؕ كُلٌّ مِّنَ الصّٰبِرِيْنَ‌ ۖ‌ۚ‏(85)\nWA ISMAA-E’ELA WAADREESA WA ZAL AL-KEFLE KULLUL MENAL MA-A’S SAABEREEN.\nAnd (remember) Isma'il, Idris, and Zul-kifl, all (men) of constancy and patience; \nوَاَدْخَلْنٰهُمْ فِىْ رَحْمَتِنَا ؕ اِنَّهُمْ مِّنَ الصّٰلِحِيْنَ‏(86)\nWAADKHALNAAHUM FEE RAHMATENAA INNAHUM MENAL SAALEHEEN.\nWe admitted them to Our mercy: for they were of the righteous ones. \nوَ ذَا النُّوْنِ اِذْ ذَّهَبَ مُغَاضِبًا فَظَنَّ اَنْ لَّنْ نَّقْدِرَ عَلَيْهِ فَنَادٰى فِى الظُّلُمٰتِ اَنْ لَّاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّاۤ اَنْتَ سُبْحٰنَكَ ‌ۖ  اِنِّىْ كُنْتُ مِنَ الظّٰلِمِيْنَ‌ ۖ ‌ۚ‏(87)\nWA ZAL AN-NOONE IZ ZZAHABA MUGHAAZEBAN FA ZANNAS AN LAN-Y NNAQDERA A’LAYHE FANAADAA FIL ZOLOMAATE AN LAA ELAAHA ILLAA ANTA SUBHAANAKA INNEE KUNTO MENAL ZAALEMEEN.\nAnd remember Zun-nun, when he departed in wrath: He imagined that We had no power over him! But he cried through the deptHs of darkness, “There is no god but thou: glory to thee: I was indeed wrong!” \nفَاسْتَجَبْنَا لَهٗۙ وَنَجَّيْنٰهُ مِنَ الْغَمِّ‌ؕ وَكَذٰلِكَ نُنْجِى الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(88)\nFAASTAJABNAA LAHU WANAJJAYNAAHU MENAL AL-GHAMME WA KAZAALEKA NUNJEAA MOAMENEEN.\nSo We listened to him: and delivered him from distress: and thus do We deliver those who have faith. \nوَزَكَرِيَّاۤ اِذْ نَادٰى رَبَّهٗ رَبِّ لَا تَذَرْنِىْ فَرْدًا وَّاَنْتَ خَيْرُ الْوٰرِثِيْنَ‌ ۖ‌ۚ‏(89)\nWAZAKAREEA IZ NAADAA WAL RABBE LAA TAZARNEAA FARDAN WWAANTA KHAYRUR WAARESEEN.\nAnd (remember) Zakariya, when he cried to his Lord: “O my Lord! leave me not without offspring, though thou art the best of inheritors.” \nفَاسْتَجَبْنَا لَهٗ وَوَهَبْنَا لَهٗ يَحْيٰى وَاَصْلَحْنَا لَهٗ زَوْجَهٗ ‌ؕ اِنَّهُمْ كَانُوْا يُسٰرِعُوْنَ فِىْ الْخَيْرٰتِ وَ يَدْعُوْنَنَا رَغَبًا وَّرَهَبًا ‌ؕ وَكَانُوْا لَنَا خٰشِعِيْنَ‏(90)\nFAASTAJABNAA LAHU WA WAHABNAA LAHU YAHYAA WAASLAHNAA LAHU ZAWJAH INNAHUM KAANOO YUSAAREU’OONA FEE AL-KHAYRAATE WA YADU’OONANAA RAGHABAN WWARAHABAN WA KAANOO LANAA KHAASHEE’EENA.\nSo We listened to him: and We granted him Yahya: We cured his wife's (Barrenness) for him. These (three) were ever quick in emulation in good works; they used to call on Us with love and reverence, and humble themselves before Us. \nوَالَّتِىْۤ اَحْصَنَتْ فَرْجَهَا فَنَفَخْنَا فِيْهَا مِنْ رُّوْحِنَا وَ جَعَلْنٰهَا وَابْنَهَاۤ اٰيَةً لِّلْعٰلَمِيْنَ‏(91)\nWA LATEE AAHSANAT FARJAHAA FANAFAKHNAA FEEHAA MIN RROOHENAA WA JA-A’LNAAHAA WAABNAHAA AAYATAL LIL-A’ALAMEEN.\nAnd (remember) her who guarded her chastity: We breathed into her of Our spirit, and We made her and her son a sign for all peoples. \nاِنَّ هٰذِهٖۤ اُمَّتُكُمْ اُمَّةً وَّاحِدَةً  ‌ۖ وَّاَنَا رَبُّكُمْ فَاعْبُدُوْنِ‏(92)\nINNAL HAAZEHI AUMMATUKUM UMMATAM WAAHEDATAN WWAANAA RABBOKUM FA’BODOON.\nVerily, this brotherhood of yours is a single brotherhood, and I am your Lord and Cherisher: therefore serve Me (and no other). \nوَتَقَطَّعُوْۤا اَمْرَهُمْ بَيْنَهُمْ‌ؕ كُلٌّ اِلَيْنَا رٰجِعُوْنَ‏(93)\nWATAQATTAU’OOA AAMRAHUM BAYNAHUM KULLUL ELAYNAA RAAJE-O’ON.\nBut (later generations) cut off their affair (of unity), one from another: (yet) will they all return to Us. \nفَمَنْ يَّعْمَلْ مِنَ الصّٰلِحٰتِ وَهُوَ مُؤْمِنٌ فَلَا كُفْرَانَ لِسَعْيِهٖ‌ۚ وَاِنَّا لَهٗ كٰتِبُوْنَ‏(94)\nFAMAN YA’MAL MENAL SAALEHAATE WA HOWA MUMENUN FALAA KUFRAANA LESAA’YEH WA INNAA LAHU KAATEBOONA.\nWhoever works any act of righteousness and has faith, His endeavour will not be rejected: We shall record it in his favour. \nوَ حَرٰمٌ عَلٰى قَرْيَةٍ اَهْلَكْنٰهَاۤ اَنَّهُمْ لَا يَرْجِعُوْنَ‏(95)\nWA HARAAMUN A’LAA QARYATINW AAHLAKNAAHAA ANNAHUM LAA YARJE-O’ON.\nBut there is a ban on any population which We have destroyed: that they shall not return, \nحَتّٰٓى اِذَا فُتِحَتْ يَاْجُوْجُ وَمَاْجُوْجُ وَهُمْ مِّنْ كُلِّ حَدَبٍ يَّنْسِلُوْنَ‏(96)\nHATTAA EZAA FUTEHAT YAAJOOJU WAMAAJOOJU WA HUM MIN KULLE HADABIN YYANSELOONA.\nUntil the Gog and Magog (people) are let through (their barrier), and they swiftly swarm from every hill. \nوَاقْتَرَبَ الْوَعْدُ الْحَقُّ فَاِذَا هِىَ شَاخِصَةٌ اَبْصَارُ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا ؕ يٰوَيْلَنَا قَدْ كُنَّا فِىْ غَفْلَةٍ مِّنْ هٰذَا بَلْ كُنَّا ظٰلِمِيْنَ‏(97)\nWAAQTARABA WA’DO HAQQO FA-EZAA HEYA SHAAKHESATUN AABSAARU LAZEENA KAFAROO YAA WAYLANAA QAD KUNNAA FEE GHAFLATIM MIN HAAZAA BAL KUNNAA ZAALEMEEN.\nThen will the true promise draw nigh (of fulfilment): then behold! the eyes of the Unbelievers will fixedly stare in horror: “Ah! Woe to us! we were indeed heedless of this; nay, we truly did wrong!” \nاِنَّكُمْ وَمَا تَعْبُدُوْنَ مِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ حَصَبُ جَهَنَّمَؕ اَنْتُمْ لَهَا وَارِدُوْنَ‏(98)\nINNAKUM WA MAA TA’BODOONA MIN DOONIL LAAHE HASABU JAHANNAM ANTUM LAHAA WAAREDOONA.\nVerily ye, (unbelievers), and the (false) gods that ye worship besides Allah, are (but) fuel for Hell! to it will ye (surely) come! \nلَوْ كَانَ هٰٓؤُلَاۤءِ اٰلِهَةً مَّا وَرَدُوْهَا‌ ؕ وَكُلٌّ فِيْهَا خٰلِدُوْنَ‏(99)\nLAW KAANA HAAOOLAAA-E AALEHATAL MAA WARADOOHAA KULLUN FEEHAA KHAALEDOON.\nIf these had been gods, they would not have got there! but each one will abide therein. \nلَهُمْ فِيْهَا زَفِيْرٌ وَّهُمْ فِيْهَا لَا يَسْمَعُوْنَ‏(100)\nLAHUM FEEHAA ZAFEERUN WA HUM FEEHAA LAA YAS-MA-O’ONA.\nThere, sobbing will be their lot, nor will they there hear (aught else). \nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ سَبَقَتْ لَهُمْ مِّنَّا الْحُسْنٰٓىۙ اُولٰٓئِكَ عَنْهَا مُبْعَدُوْنَۙ‏(101)\nINNAL LAZEENA SABAQAT LAHUM MINNAA AL-HUSNAAA OOLAAA-EKA A’NHAA MUBA’ADOONA.\nThose for whom the good (record) from Us has gone before, will be removed far therefrom. \nلَا يَسْمَعُوْنَ حَسِيْسَهَا‌ ۚ وَهُمْ فِىْ مَا اشْتَهَتْ اَنْفُسُهُمْ خٰلِدُوْنَ‌ ۚ‏(102)\nLAA YAS-MA-O’ONA HASEESAHAA WA HUM FEE MAA ASHTAHAT ANFOSOHUM KHAALEDOON.\nNot the slightest sound will they hear of Hell: what their souls desired, in that will they dwell. \nلَا يَحْزُنُهُمُ الْفَزَعُ الْاَكْبَرُ وَتَتَلَقّٰٮهُمُ الْمَلٰٓئِكَةُ ؕ هٰذَا يَوْمُكُمُ الَّذِىْ كُنْتُمْ تُوْعَدُوْنَ‏(103)\nLAA YAHZUNUHUMU AL-FAZAU’U AL-AAKBARU WATATALAQQAAHUMU TAHMELOHUL HAAZAA YAWMUKUMU LAZEE KUNTUM TOO-A’DOON.\nThe Great Terror will bring them no grief: but the angels will meet them (with mutual greetings): “This is your Day, (the Day) that ye were promised.” \nيَوْمَ نَطْوِىْ السَّمَآءَ كَطَىِّ السِّجِلِّ لِلْكُتُبِ‌ ؕ كَمَا بَدَاْنَاۤ اَوَّلَ خَلْقٍ نُّعِيْدُهٗ‌ ؕ وَعْدًا عَلَيْنَا‌ ؕ اِنَّا كُنَّا فٰعِلِيْنَ‏(104)\nYAWMA NATWEAA SAMAAA-AD KATAA AS-SEJELLE LIL-KUTUBE KAMAA BADAANAA AWWALA KHALQIN NNUE’EEDUH WA’DAN A’LAYNAA INNAA KUNNAA FAAE’ELEENA.\nThe Day that We roll up the heavens like a scroll rolled up for books (completed), even as We produced the first creation, so shall We produce a new one: a promise We have undertaken: truly shall We fulfil it. \nوَلَقَدْ كَتَبْنَا فِى الزَّبُوْرِ مِنْۢ بَعْدِ الذِّكْرِ اَنَّ الْاَرْضَ يَرِثُهَا عِبَادِىَ الصّٰلِحُوْنَ‏(105)\nWA LAQAD KATABNAA FIL AZ-ZABOORE MIN BA’DE AZ-ZEKRE ANNAL ARZA YARESUHAA E’EBAADEAAA AS-SAALEHOONA.\nBefore this We wrote in the Psalms, after the Message (given to Moses): My servants the righteous, shall inherit the earth.” \nاِنَّ فِىْ هٰذَا لَبَلٰغًا لِّقَوْمٍ عٰبِدِيْنَؕ‏(106)\nINNAL FEE HAAZAA LABALAAGHAN LEQAWMINY A’AABEDEENA.\nVerily in this (Qur'an) is a Message for people who would (truly) worship Allah. \nوَمَاۤ اَرْسَلْنٰكَ اِلَّا رَحْمَةً لِّلْعٰلَمِيْنَ‏(107)\nWA MAA ARSALNAAKA ILLAA RAHMATAM LIL-A’ALAMEEN.\nWe sent thee not, but as a Mercy for all creatures. \nقُلْ اِنَّمَا يُوْحٰۤى اِلَىَّ اَنَّمَاۤ اِلٰهُكُمْ اِلٰهٌ وَّاحِدٌ‌  ۚ فَهَلْ اَنْتُمْ مُّسْلِمُوْنَ‏(108)\nQUL INNAMAA YOOHAA ELAYYA ANNAMAA ELAAHOKUM ELAAHUN WAAHED FA HAL ANTUM MUSLEMOON.\nSay: “What has come to me by inspiration is that your Allah is One Allah: will ye therefore bow to His Will (in Islam)?” \nفَاِنْ تَوَلَّوْا فَقُلْ اٰذَنْتُكُمْ عَلٰى سَوَآءٍ ‌ؕ وَاِنْ اَدْرِىْۤ اَقَرِيْبٌ اَمْ بَعِيْدٌ مَّا تُوْعَدُوْنَ‏(109)\nFA-IN TAWALLAW FAQUL AAAZANTUKUM A’LAA SAWAAIN WA AADREAA AAQAREEBUN AM BAE’EEDUN MAA TOO-A’DOON.\nBut if they turn back, Say: “I have proclaimed the Message to you all alike and in truth; but I know not whether that which ye are promised is near or far. \nاِنَّهٗ يَعْلَمُ الْجَهْرَ مِنَ الْقَوْلِ وَيَعْلَمُ مَا تَكْتُمُوْنَ‏(110)\nINNAHU YA’LAMO JAHRA MENAL AL-QAWLE YA’LAMO MAA TAKTOMOON.\n“It is He Who knows what is open in speech and what ye hide (in your hearts). \nوَاِنْ اَدْرِىْ لَعَلَّهٗ فِتْنَةٌ لَّكُمْ وَمَتَاعٌ اِلٰى حِيْنٍ‏(111)\nWA AADREAA LA-A’LLAHU FITNATUN LAKUM WA LIL-MOTAALLAQAATE ELAA HEEN.\n“I know not but that it may be a trial for you, and a grant of (worldly) livelihood (to you) for a time.” \nقٰلَ رَبِّ احْكُمْ بِالْحَقِّ‌ؕ وَرَبُّنَا الرَّحْمٰنُ الْمُسْتَعَانُ عَلٰى مَا تَصِفُوْنَ‏(112)\nQAALA RABBE AHKUM BIL-HAQ WA RABBONAA RAHMAANO AL-MUSTAA’AANU A’LAA MAA TASEFOONA.\nSay: “O my Lord! judge Thou in truth!” “Our Lord Most Gracious is the One Whose assistance should be sought against the blasphemies ye utter!” ",
  "merits": "Surah al-Anbiyaa (The Prophets)\nThis ‘Makki’ Surah has 112 verses. It is narrated that the reward for reciting this Surah is that the accounting on the Day of Reckoning becomes easy for the reciter and all the Prophets whose names appear in the Holy Qur’an will come to meet him on this day.\nImam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) has said that whoever recites Surah al-Anbiyaa frequently, his status in Paradise will be close to the Prophets. Writing this Surah and keeping it with one removes all stress and worry."
}
